# Base Frame — photo selection manifest
# Lists ONLY the shots we keep, and what each becomes in the guide.
# Format:  SOURCE.HEIC   target.jpg      (# comments + blank lines ignored)
# Convert with (macOS):
#   tools/convert-build-photos.sh <staging-dir> docs/assets/build/base-frame/photos.manifest docs/assets/build/base-frame
# Convert with (any OS — needs `pip install pillow pillow-heif`):
#   python3 tools/convert_build_photos.py <staging-dir> docs/assets/build/base-frame/photos.manifest docs/assets/build/base-frame
# That holds every output under the 300 KB target in docs/assets/build/README.md,
# stepping quality down and then shrinking if needed. No flags required.
#
# Source: the "1 - Base Frame Build" Drive folder. Sources are numbered in build
# order; the "done" suffix marks the completed-frame shots.

# --- Step 1 — rails and parts laid out ---
1.jpeg           01-long-rail.jpg
2.jpeg           01-cross-rail.jpg
6.jpg            01-parts-laid-out.jpg

